Z||000005||Seanh||01-17-2001||10:07 PM||||What a rip off!!! The reason I say that is, most Fiero folks buy aftermarket spings to lower the car, the added stiffness is just an added benefit. Here is, IMO, the best lowring kit on the market today, and alot cheaper then those spings: <A HREF="http://www.84to96.net/kaleco/appear.htm" TARGET=_blank>KALECO</A>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> J/K <BR>That is, I must admit, a pretty good price for a complete set. I mean, look at the Fiero store's price for a pair. I just bought a coil-over set from Mike or I would probally go for these. I would be interested in those F-1 brakes though. I have hella-trouble stoping my car now. Could you check and see if you can get F-1 brakes? If so, are they compatable with my recent addition of cross drilled brake lines? <A HREF="http://www.84to96.net/kaleco/performance.htm" TARGET=_blank>Here's the specs for the cross drilled lines</A><BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto (3.4 Conversion in Progress)<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I>||||reg||1
