Z||000010||ArmandoP||01-18-2001||01:08 PM||||ok guys, enough with the MR2 bashing.....<BR>atleast while Im here...pleeease.<P>thats ALOT of fendergap!!!<P>as afr as I know, I cannot get F1 brakes, though I wioll look into some of the stuff thats available as soon as this GP is over.<P>payment...<BR>I have a mailing list Im using to update people on the progress of the GP.  email me to get on it, pplease, this is the best way to stay informed.<BR>ok, I can take check, MO or crdit card through paypal.  I can understand why youd be wary of paying me especially because of the whole cutter ordeal, but I guarantee you, I have been selling parts on my own for quite some time and have NEVER stiffed anyone.  Intrax will not sell direct to the public.  in fact, to get these prices, I had to get a distributorship from them!  nobody else would sell them cheaper.<BR>As far as indiana and illinois shipping goes...I or my business partner (Mike Ryan) will HAND DELIVER the parts to your door!!!  If youre not in indiana or illinois, you WILL get a tracking number.  If shipping turns out to be less than $10, you will recieve a refund of the difference with the springs, if it is more than $10, you only pay $10.<BR>Ive wanted to start a motorsports company for a long time due to the lack of MKI MR2 parts available, and when I couldnt get a good price on intrax springs it was the perfect opportunity.  Mike and I (CrazyRhyno Motorsports)are fabricating parts for the MR2, and I see no reason why we couldnt make parts for the Fiero.  We both own cars that are not exactly common, and share the same mid engine platform, theres no reason, especially when you have so much to gain here, to be talking crap.<BR>I would be happy to fabricate hard to get fiero parts along side hard to find mr2 parts, but you guys, please, dont talk **** .<BR>Im trying real hard ot to offer this GP to the clubsi people because theyre dicks...if you guys work with me, I can make sure I dont have to offer it to them in order to get the required 30 sets.<BR>Armando<BR>87MR2<BR>93 Del Sol (Becky's)<BR>84 fiero (becky's brother)<BR>86 fiero (Becky;'s brother)<P>------------------<BR>__________________<BR>will work for MR2 parts!!! <BR>1987 MR2 NA t-bar csp with 700 miles on its new engine. <BR>TRD copper head gasket, milled head .020, 2 short shifters,metal masters rear brake pads, 195-60-14 (soon to get new tires), clear corners, Clevite 77 bearings, NO A/C, MAF relocation mod, red silicon vacuum hoses, redline tranny fluid,and the stock exhaust with a WHOLE bunch of broken welds! <BR>indiana/illinois MR2 owners club<BR>[URLhttp://php.indiana.edu/~ajperez/inimoc.html[/URL]<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://php.indiana.edu/~ajperez/mytwo.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by ArmandoP (edited 01-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Greg Piet||01-18-2001||03:43 PM||||Dont get agitated at these questions, but I feel an answer is necessary to properly know what one is purchasing.<P>Progressive rate springs?<BR>Normally there is some spring stiffness value even on progresive rate to know which springs are "beefier".<BR>ex: ST about 130<BR>Eibach about 190<BR>thus Eibachs are much stiffer...<BR>what are these?<BR><P>------------------<BR>SCCA Region 72<BR>#47 CSP<BR>Bring it to the track.<BR>Lets see if all those mods really helped!||||reg||1
